1
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:13,931
Giant animals, living legends.

2
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,185
Fantastic creatures.

3
00:00:19,353 --> 00:00:23,190
These are nature's big beasts.

4
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:27,486
But experience the world
from their perspective,

5
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:32,406
and you'll see it's not easy being huge.

6
00:00:34,493 --> 00:00:36,662
The larger the animal,

7
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:38,497
the higher the stakes

8
00:00:39,206 --> 00:00:41,834
and the more epic the adventure.

9
00:00:55,222 --> 00:00:58,058
It's exhausting being a dad…

10
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:05,399
especially if you're responsible
for the largest eggs in the world.

11
00:01:07,943 --> 00:01:10,779
Each the size of a coconut.

12
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:18,745
And 30 times the weight of a chicken egg.

13
00:01:22,541 --> 00:01:26,503
He's tended them 16 hours a day
for five weeks.

14
00:01:30,674 --> 00:01:33,844
Just one more until they hatch.

15
00:01:38,015 --> 00:01:40,350
When it comes to father figures,

16
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:44,062
ostriches are outstanding.

17
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:47,941
Nine feet tall, in fact.

18
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:54,990
But the world's biggest bird
needs a lot of food.

19
00:01:56,992 --> 00:01:57,993
When hunger calls…

20
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:06,502
he must leave his eggs to go and eat.

21
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:16,178
Finding five pounds of plants a day
is easy here.

22
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:22,893
This is a paradise for all sorts
of gigantic grazers.

23
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:28,190
From the tallest…

24
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:39,034
to the heaviest animals to walk the Earth.

25
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:46,959
But raising a family in a land of giants
is a huge challenge.

26
00:03:01,849 --> 00:03:03,267
On the African savanna,

27
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:07,855
the bigger you are,
the better your chances…

28
00:03:13,068 --> 00:03:17,281
against the large carnivores
that patrol the plains.

29
00:03:24,538 --> 00:03:29,334
It takes a brave lion
to tackle a full-grown giraffe.

30
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:35,591
Even a male ostrich is relatively safe.

31
00:03:40,804 --> 00:03:43,724
Still, he must watch out for danger

32
00:03:45,017 --> 00:03:48,103
with the largest eyes of any bird.

33
00:03:54,902 --> 00:03:58,197
Unfortunately,
they're bigger than his brain.

34
00:04:01,325 --> 00:04:03,660
And he's easily distracted.

35
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:10,042
But lose focus for a moment,

36
00:04:10,709 --> 00:04:13,462
and you could lose it all.

37
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:33,023
His future family destroyed.

38
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:41,365
The poor ostrich will have to start again.

39
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:48,038
And he's running out of time
before the breeding season ends.

40
00:05:01,677 --> 00:05:04,763
With so many animals grazing
on the savanna,

41
00:05:05,389 --> 00:05:09,935
superior size gives an advantage
over the competition.

42
00:05:18,652 --> 00:05:21,530
Standing 17 feet tall…

43
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:28,412
giraffes can reach the plants
others can't.

44
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:35,419
Browsing the treetops,
they pick the tastiest tips

45
00:05:35,919 --> 00:05:39,089
with their dexterous 18-inch tongues.

46
00:05:49,308 --> 00:05:53,562
But exclusive dining comes at a cost.

47
00:05:55,564 --> 00:05:58,817
It takes a heart the size of
two bowling balls

48
00:05:58,901 --> 00:06:01,320
to circulate blood up to their heads

49
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:06,283
and a lot of fuel to keep it pumping.

50
00:06:09,119 --> 00:06:11,788
Eating over a hundred pounds of leaves
a day

51
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:15,959
means spending up to 12 hours
head-in-the-trees.

52
00:06:18,504 --> 00:06:23,050
Not easy when you have someone else
to look out for.

53
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:27,930
Her brand-new calf.

54
00:06:31,975 --> 00:06:37,940
Already six feet tall with
the umbilical cord still attached…

55
00:06:44,571 --> 00:06:47,241
and still finding his feet.

56
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:59,378
The taller the animal,
the longer it takes for its brain

57
00:07:00,003 --> 00:07:01,380
to talk to its legs.

58
00:07:09,805 --> 00:07:12,808
At least he's got
the important things licked,

59
00:07:13,725 --> 00:07:15,936
and he'll soon grow into that neck.

60
00:07:17,187 --> 00:07:20,148
At first, he adds an inch every day.

61
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:25,362
Within four years
he'll be almost full height

62
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:27,573
and able to stand up for himself

63
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,867
amongst the big boys.

64
00:07:35,539 --> 00:07:37,833
For now he'll join the family crèche…

65
00:07:39,835 --> 00:07:43,881
a safe place to learn and play.

66
00:07:51,013 --> 00:07:56,560
With one of the moms watching over him,
he's free to explore.

67
00:08:05,277 --> 00:08:08,280
As long as he stays within sight.

68
00:08:11,867 --> 00:08:16,288
A giraffe's huge eyes
see almost 300 degrees.

69
00:08:19,875 --> 00:08:24,213
From up here, she can spot trouble
a mile off.

70
00:08:27,299 --> 00:08:29,718
No wonder she's so skittish.

71
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:36,475
When Africa's biggest cat attacks,

72
00:08:37,851 --> 00:08:39,602
most animals run.

73
00:08:52,199 --> 00:08:55,827
But some stand their ground.

74
00:09:19,685 --> 00:09:22,813
1,500 pounds.

75
00:09:23,814 --> 00:09:25,357
Two-foot horns.

76
00:09:26,233 --> 00:09:27,943
An inch-thick hide.

77
00:09:30,779 --> 00:09:33,574
Millions of years battling big cats

78
00:09:33,657 --> 00:09:37,286
has forced buffaloes to supersize.

79
00:09:40,122 --> 00:09:43,333
A single buffalo
can inflict serious injuries.

80
00:09:45,043 --> 00:09:50,591
And when the herd stands together,
they're more than a match for a lion.

81
00:09:54,344 --> 00:09:55,345
But they'll be back.

82
00:09:57,055 --> 00:09:58,515
And hunting as a pride,

83
00:09:59,016 --> 00:10:01,894
they'll become a force
to be reckoned with.

84
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:25,334
Flushed red with testosterone
and strutting his stuff,

85
00:10:26,168 --> 00:10:30,255
the male ostrich is in peak condition.

86
00:10:33,258 --> 00:10:35,052
After losing his clutch of eggs,

87
00:10:35,135 --> 00:10:38,555
he must move fast
to win round his females.

88
00:10:52,236 --> 00:10:56,615
Long, powerful legs can cover 12 feet

89
00:10:57,282 --> 00:10:58,951
in a single stride.

90
00:11:02,329 --> 00:11:04,623
At up to 45 miles an hour,

91
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:09,086
he's twice as fast as Usain Bolt.

92
00:11:12,381 --> 00:11:15,008
It shows he's got stamina.

93
00:11:19,596 --> 00:11:23,225
But his hens need convincing.

94
00:11:25,394 --> 00:11:29,815
Sure, he can move. But can he really move?

95
00:11:44,246 --> 00:11:49,793
A male needs to dance
if he wants to bring the females flocking.

96
00:11:53,255 --> 00:11:58,635
And now, he has four hens to satisfy.

97
00:12:07,686 --> 00:12:11,481
Thankfully, mating is a brief affair.

98
00:12:20,824 --> 00:12:24,286
Five days later,
the females are ready to lay.

99
00:12:28,624 --> 00:12:31,376
His major hen goes first.

100
00:12:39,301 --> 00:12:40,844
Then, others follow.

101
00:12:48,685 --> 00:12:53,774
Up to 50 eggs in total
in a nest ten feet wide.

102
00:13:05,994 --> 00:13:09,373
Eighty percent are usually
lost to predators

103
00:13:10,165 --> 00:13:11,583
or to the baking sun.

104
00:13:14,545 --> 00:13:17,089
Those in the middle, the safest.

105
00:13:17,798 --> 00:13:23,345
And incredibly, it seems females can tell
which are theirs.

106
00:13:24,555 --> 00:13:28,475
So, the major hen makes sure
her eggs are in the best spot,

107
00:13:29,935 --> 00:13:32,646
leaving the others to fight it out.

108
00:13:34,189 --> 00:13:39,736
But ultimately, the fate
of the next generation rests with dad.

109
00:13:40,654 --> 00:13:43,323
What could possibly go wrong?

110
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:57,045
By midsummer,
the sun is at its most powerful.

111
00:14:02,134 --> 00:14:06,346
The bigger the animal,
the more it struggles to lose heat

112
00:14:07,306 --> 00:14:09,183
and keep hydrated.

113
00:14:13,562 --> 00:14:18,650
Most of the year, giraffes get all of
their water from the leaves they eat.

114
00:14:20,861 --> 00:14:26,158
But now they must follow the crowds
traveling down to the river.

115
00:14:43,175 --> 00:14:48,180
Arriving together helps protect against
waiting predators.

116
00:14:51,850 --> 00:14:55,562
Even so, drinking 15 pints a day
isn't easy…

117
00:14:58,232 --> 00:14:59,733
when you're being watched.

118
00:15:03,529 --> 00:15:08,200
A thirsty giraffe faces
a more basic challenge.

119
00:15:12,996 --> 00:15:15,499
Being tall may make eating easy,

120
00:15:16,583 --> 00:15:19,336
but drinking is difficult.

121
00:15:20,921 --> 00:15:23,131
It's such a long way down.

122
00:15:29,304 --> 00:15:32,266
Giraffes have special valves
in their necks

123
00:15:32,349 --> 00:15:35,727
to prevent passing out
from a rush of blood to the head.

124
00:15:40,399 --> 00:15:44,653
And what look like knees
are actually ankles.

125
00:15:49,241 --> 00:15:54,204
The more they bend, the more toppling
over becomes a real concern…

126
00:15:57,082 --> 00:15:59,168
especially for youngsters.

127
00:16:07,134 --> 00:16:10,220
But lookouts can't be everywhere at once.

128
00:16:17,895 --> 00:16:23,108
When the giraffe's head is down,
it doesn't spot danger so easily.

129
00:17:22,376 --> 00:17:26,797
Thankfully, those lanky legs are good
for running.

130
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:36,557
Now, it's the lions who need to watch
their back.

131
00:17:40,143 --> 00:17:42,813
The buffaloes see to that.

132
00:17:58,495 --> 00:18:02,791
Finally, everyone can drink in peace.

133
00:18:06,128 --> 00:18:07,880
Well, almost.

134
00:18:09,548 --> 00:18:12,926
The male ostrich just has to sit it out,

135
00:18:14,303 --> 00:18:20,225
baking in the 100-degree heat
to ensure his eggs don't.

136
00:18:24,938 --> 00:18:27,524
The major hen helps him brood.

137
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:35,365
If nothing else, to make sure
her eggs remain in prime position.

138
00:18:42,164 --> 00:18:45,417
She even joins him, fanning the nest.

139
00:18:48,128 --> 00:18:51,089
Dad seems more on the ball this time.

140
00:18:52,716 --> 00:18:54,551
On top of incubation duties…

141
00:18:56,929 --> 00:19:00,057
and warier of predators.

142
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:06,688
A month in, and things are looking up.

143
00:19:17,032 --> 00:19:19,076
The rains have arrived.

144
00:19:39,888 --> 00:19:43,600
Take fertile soil, soak in water,

145
00:19:44,184 --> 00:19:46,103
bathe in tropical sun,

146
00:19:46,687 --> 00:19:51,191
and the savanna becomes one
of the most abundant places on Earth.

147
00:19:53,569 --> 00:19:57,698
Enough grass grows to feed an invasion.

148
00:19:59,783 --> 00:20:02,202
Huge herds,

149
00:20:02,286 --> 00:20:05,998
and even more enormous animals.

150
00:20:10,377 --> 00:20:14,756
Elephants need up to
300 pounds of plants a day…

151
00:20:17,509 --> 00:20:19,469
so they follow the rains.

152
00:20:24,516 --> 00:20:29,062
Every step crushing with the weight
of three pickup trucks.

153
00:20:39,031 --> 00:20:42,492
Where titans tread,
smaller creatures usually scatter.

154
00:20:46,538 --> 00:20:50,292
But carmine bee-eaters see opportunity.

155
00:20:53,545 --> 00:20:58,133
They know it pays to follow
in the footsteps of giants.

156
00:21:04,473 --> 00:21:07,267
As the elephants flush
insects out of hiding…

157
00:21:11,939 --> 00:21:14,399
the little birds pick them off.

158
00:21:31,708 --> 00:21:34,586
Elephants aren't the only ones
worth following.

159
00:21:41,677 --> 00:21:44,513
Sometimes, the boldest bee-eaters

160
00:21:44,596 --> 00:21:49,726
even hitch a lift on birds 2,000 times
their weight.

161
00:21:54,439 --> 00:21:58,527
Though not every ostrich
likes being taken for a ride.

162
00:22:05,492 --> 00:22:10,247
Never mind. There's always another giant
passing by.

163
00:22:13,208 --> 00:22:17,379
And bee-eaters aren't the only ones
to flock around giraffes.

164
00:22:19,214 --> 00:22:22,259
Oxpeckers also cling on,

165
00:22:23,302 --> 00:22:26,096
feasting on parasites in their fur.

166
00:22:29,266 --> 00:22:33,937
It seems the higher you rise,
the greater your entourage,

167
00:22:35,522 --> 00:22:39,902
and your influence
on the landscape around you.

168
00:22:44,239 --> 00:22:48,452
As giraffes feed, they carry pollen
from flower to flower,

169
00:22:48,535 --> 00:22:51,830
like 17-foot-tall bees.

170
00:22:55,626 --> 00:22:57,586
Securing the future of the savanna

171
00:22:58,629 --> 00:23:01,798
for the next generation of giraffes.

172
00:23:07,054 --> 00:23:09,640
The youngster is growing up fast,

173
00:23:11,517 --> 00:23:14,269
and Mum can be a little more relaxed.

174
00:23:20,609 --> 00:23:24,154
Now, he's big enough.
It's time to join the herd.

175
00:23:33,038 --> 00:23:37,042
The ostrich dad's devotion has paid off.

176
00:23:41,129 --> 00:23:42,256
At last,

177
00:23:43,006 --> 00:23:45,843
he is the proud father of a new brood.

178
00:24:03,777 --> 00:24:07,906
The hatchlings are already
the size of a chicken,

179
00:24:09,616 --> 00:24:12,703
but still, with a long way to grow.

180
00:24:14,830 --> 00:24:17,249
They'll gain 12 inches a month at first.

181
00:24:20,085 --> 00:24:24,214
In a year and a half, they'll weigh
as much as a refrigerator…

182
00:24:26,967 --> 00:24:29,386
and be almost full height.

183
00:24:32,306 --> 00:24:35,184
There's lots to learn before then.

184
00:24:38,228 --> 00:24:42,649
But Dad will be there
to show them the way.

185
00:24:45,861 --> 00:24:49,364
Ostrich fathers stay with their chicks
for up to a year,

186
00:24:50,032 --> 00:24:53,410
one of the longest paternal investments
of any bird.

187
00:24:54,703 --> 00:24:59,166
Raising such a large family
is a massive responsibility,

188
00:25:00,626 --> 00:25:07,007
but he's well on his way to becoming
one of the greatest animal dads of all.

